Package: dimsprepr
Title: End-to-End Preprocessing of Direct-Injection Metabolomics Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R:
    person("John Lennon", "Calorio", , "jllcalorio@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A complete, reproducible preprocessing pipeline for
    direct-injection mass spectrometry (DIMS) metabolomics data: blank
    filtering, missing value filtering, quality control (QC) based signal
    drift and batch correction (Kirwan et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1007/s00216-013-6856-7>), including the outlier-robust methods of
    Vynck et al. (2026) <doi:10.1021/acs.analchem.5c06841>, imputation,
    normalization including probabilistic quotient normalization (Dieterle
    et al. (2006) <doi:10.1021/ac051632c>), transformation, scaling (van den
    Berg et al. (2006) <doi:10.1186/1471-2164-7-142>), and QC-based quality
    filtering (Broadhurst et al. (2018) <doi:10.1007/s11306-018-1367-3>),
    following the QComics guidelines (Gonzalez-Dominguez et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.1021/acs.analchem.3c03660>). Supports multi-method mode:
    normalization, transformation, and scaling methods may each be supplied
    as character vectors, and the pipeline computes every combination while
    running the shared preprocessing steps only once.
